Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:58:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: Keep SIM PIN bouncer visible on heads-up

For a SIM PIN or PUK the keyguard is hidden behind the bouncer, so the
status bar state is SHADE and the panel counts as fully collapsed. A
heads-up pinned then (e.g. "USB debugging connected" right after boot)
calls updateTouchableRegion(), which sets forceWindowCollapsed for one
frame. isExpanded() let that override keyguard and bouncer, so the whole
notification shade window went invisible and the bouncer blinked.

Ignore forceWindowCollapsed while the keyguard or the bouncer is showing;
the window is full screen in those states anyway.

Assisted-by: LLM
Change-Id: I078e979021fce8b183bf512f8615216e760e7224
---
 .../shade/NotificationShadeWindowControllerImpl.java         | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/shade/NotificationShadeWindowControllerImpl.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/shade/NotificationShadeWindowControllerImpl.java
index 6232ded3e8a9e..f17db3294b891 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/shade/NotificationShadeWindowControllerImpl.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/shade/NotificationShadeWindowControllerImpl.java
@@ -514,8 +514,9 @@ private void applyVisibility(NotificationShadeWindowState state) {
     }
 
     private boolean isExpanded(NotificationShadeWindowState state) {
-        boolean isExpanded = !state.forceWindowCollapsed && (state.isKeyguardShowingAndNotOccluded()
-                || state.panelVisible || state.keyguardFadingAway || state.bouncerShowing
+        // forceWindowCollapsed must not hide keyguard or bouncer, e.g. the SIM PIN bouncer.
+        boolean isExpanded = state.isKeyguardShowingAndNotOccluded() || state.bouncerShowing
+                || !state.forceWindowCollapsed && (state.panelVisible || state.keyguardFadingAway
                 || state.headsUpNotificationShowing
                 || state.scrimsVisibility != ScrimController.TRANSPARENT)
                 || state.backgroundBlurRadius > 0
